AArch64 SpinlockSwp3
(* Spinlock as compiled from C++/Rust (Promising-ARM PLDI'19 §7 "SLC/SLR"),
   test-and-test-and-set shape: `while (lock.exchange(1, acquire)) { while
   (lock.load(relaxed)) {} }` -- SWPA to acquire, LDR spin while held, STLR
   release. (A bare SWPA spin loop has an infinite state space in the
   promising machine: every failed swap appends a new message.)
   Three threads each take the lock once and increment a shared counter.
   Property: counter = 3 in every final state. Expected: Always.
   Proved for all layouts and any number of threads, the runner's whole
   image (`A64WholeCounters.runnerWhole`): `SwpInv.swp_counter_armv8`
   (Promising/SLR/SwpFinal.lean), `SwpPublic.swp_counter_public`
   (Promising/SLR/SwpPublic.lean); at `decls = {}`, on the pre-EnvG cell
   route. No fault at `decls = {}`: `SwpInv.swpRuleX_noFault`
   (Promising/SLR/SwpNoFault.lean).
   The shared symbols are typed (`uint32_t lock`, `uint32_t counter`, the width of every access)
   so that the runner declares them as sized locations at the width of
   the code's accesses (A64DECLS): the runner's
   declarations then agree with the proofs' locations. The code block and
   the verdict are unchanged.
   The runner-exact theorem and the no-fault at the runner's declarations
   are proved by a new EnvG proof with the statement
   of `swp_counter_public` (SWPRUN): `SwpEnvG.swp_counter_envG`
   (Promising/SLR/EnvG/SwpEnvGPublic.lean). Proved from the runner's exact
   configuration (declarations and initial memory included):
   `swp_counter_envG_runner`, concrete `swp_counter_envG_runner_concrete3`
   (Promising/SLR/EnvG/A64SwpRunner.lean).
   Proved no fault at the runner's declarations (each access resolves as
   at `decls = {}`): `swp_counter_envG_runner_noFault`, concrete
   `swp_counter_envG_runner_noFault_concrete` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/A64SwpNoFault.lean).
   Proved program-level fault freedom at the runner's declarations (no
   reachable configuration has a faulting step, any architecture, promises
   included): `swp_counter_envG_runner_faultFree`, concrete
   `swp_counter_envG_runner_faultFree_concreteN 3` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/A64SwpNoFault.lean).
   Proved (LIVESPIN2): promise-free deadlock-freedom on a valid layout,
   `Live.SpinSwpFam.spin_swp_live_pf [ValidLayout (layout swpWorker)] : SwpSpinLivePF fuel`,
   concrete `spin_swp_live_pf_concrete`; per-thread liveness of these one-shot
   workers `spin_swp_live_oneShot_pf` (Promising/LiveSpinSwpFam.lean). With
   promises (`SwpSpinLive`) open (KNOWN_GAPS.md, "Liveness: spinlocks (LIVESPIN)").
   Proved (LIVESPINSEM2): with promises and semantic certification,
   `Live.SpinSemSwpLive.spin_swp_live_sem [ValidLayout (layout swpWorker)] : SwpSpinLiveSem fuel`
   for every fuel, concrete `spin_swp_live_sem_concrete`, and the one-shot
   `spin_swp_live_oneShot_sem` (Promising/LiveSpinSemSwpLive.lean). `SwpSpinLive`
   (over `succs`) stays open (KNOWN_GAPS.md). *)
# flags: -sym
# expect: Always
{
uint32_t lock=0; uint32_t counter=0;
0:X0=lock; 0:X1=counter;
1:X0=lock; 1:X1=counter;
2:X0=lock; 2:X1=counter;
}
threads { P0: worker done; P1: worker done; P2: worker done; }
code {
worker:
  MOV W3,#1
try:
  SWPA W3,W2,[X0]
  CBZ W2,cs
spin:
  LDR W2,[X0]
  CBNZ W2,spin
  B try
cs:
  LDR W5,[X1]
  ADD W5,W5,#1
  STR W5,[X1]
  STLR WZR,[X0]
  B done
done:
}
forall [counter]=3
